`TrainerConfig` regularises fine-tuning. `backbone_dropout` sets every dropout outside the head, including the attention dropouts that torch's and braindecode's attention modules keep as a number, and REVE, which has no dropout, refuses it. `head_dropout` puts a dropout on the input of the head and sets those inside it. `head_weight_decay` gives the head its own AdamW weight decay. Each defaults to `None`, which changes nothing, and can be tuned with a grid such as `trainer__head_dropout`. `CheckpointConfig(save_features=True)` writes, after each outer fold's fit, the fine-tuned embeddings of that fold's training and test windows next to its checkpoint, as `<checkpoint>_features.npz`: float32 `features`, `sample_id`, `y`, `group`, `split` (`"train"`, `"valid"` for the groups held out for early stopping, or `"test"`) and `fold`. `FoundationClassifier.transform` returns these embeddings, which for CTNet, Deep4Net, EEGNet and ShallowFBCSPNet are the flattened input of their final layer.
